<workout_file><author>mywhooshinfo.com</author><name>Explosive Climb</name><description>You are attacking your way into the base of the long climbs today. By completing a high-powered effort at the bottom of the climb, you will build up lactate, becoming the predominant fuel source. 

But the main focus today is on completing very long, low cadence efforts.</description><sportType>bike</sportType><workout>
<Warmup  Duration="420" PowerLow="0.454499989748" PowerHigh="0.75449997186661"><textevent timeoffset="40" message="A gradual warmup today as the intensity of the session isn&#039;t overly hard."/><textevent timeoffset="240" message="This means sub-threshold power at a lower than normal cadence."/><textevent timeoffset="300" message="The only way to train for this is by completing long efforts."/><textevent timeoffset="360" message="But today we add to the training effect by completing some high intensity surges before the &#039;climbing&#039; efforts."/><textevent timeoffset="400" message="To complete the warmup we go straight into a threshold effort."/></Warmup>
<SteadyState  Duration="180" Power="0.95450001955032"><textevent timeoffset="60" message="Self select your cadence for this effort."/><textevent timeoffset="120" message="The low cadence work is ahead."/></SteadyState>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.50449997186661"><textevent timeoffset="100" message="A good rest period now. The hard work is long today!"/><textevent timeoffset="240" message="To build some fatigue in the legs we open with 3 x 15sec high powered efforts."/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="Then straight into the low cadence work."/><textevent timeoffset="280" message="Here we go."/></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="3" OnDuration="15" OnPower="1.5045000314713" OffDuration="15" OffPower="0.65450000762939">
</IntervalsT>
<Warmup  Cadence="75" Duration="900" PowerLow="0.80449998378754" PowerHigh="0.92449998855591"><textevent timeoffset="10" message="Go straight for the target cadence of 75rpm."/><textevent timeoffset="70" message="Settle in for a long effort."/><textevent timeoffset="130" message="The target power will gradually increase."/><textevent timeoffset="190" message="Just keep the revs at 75 and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="310" message="Relieve the pressure in your legs occasionally by getting out of the seat for a few pedal strokes."/><textevent timeoffset="370" message="Into the upper end of zone 3 now."/><textevent timeoffset="430" message="You&#039;re doing a great job."/><textevent timeoffset="490" message="Long intervals are juts like long climbs."/><textevent timeoffset="510" message="They take good concentration."/><textevent timeoffset="570" message="You should be able to maintain the target cadence without watching the data on the screen."/><textevent timeoffset="630" message="This demonstrates a good &#039;feeling&#039; for the effort."/><textevent timeoffset="780" message="Just 2min to go. Almost at the top"/><textevent timeoffset="880" message="Great work. That completes the first long climb."/></Warmup>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.5"><textevent timeoffset="100" message="Another good recovery period now."/><textevent timeoffset="220" message="In the next long effort we increase the target cadence to 80rpm."/><textevent timeoffset="280" message="But first we have the high intensity 15sec efforts!"/></SteadyState>
<IntervalsT   Repeat="3" OnDuration="15" OnPower="1.5045000314713" OffDuration="15" OffPower="0.65450000762939">
</IntervalsT>
<Cooldown  Cadence="80" Duration="900" PowerLow="0.92449998855591" PowerHigh="0.80449998378754"><textevent timeoffset="70" message="Settle in for a long effort."/><textevent timeoffset="130" message="The good news is this time we start with the high power and gradually reduce the target power."/><textevent timeoffset="190" message="Just keep the revs at 80 and let the smart trainer adjust the power."/><textevent timeoffset="310" message="Relieve the pressure in your legs occasionally by getting out of the seat for a few pedal strokes."/><textevent timeoffset="370" message="This effort simulates starting a long climb a little quick and having to back the power off."/><textevent timeoffset="430" message="You&#039;re doing a great job."/><textevent timeoffset="490" message="Long intervals are juts like long climbs."/><textevent timeoffset="510" message="They take good concentration."/><textevent timeoffset="570" message="You should be able to maintain the target cadence without watching the data on the screen."/><textevent timeoffset="630" message="This demonstrates a good &#039;feeling&#039; for the effort."/><textevent timeoffset="780" message="Just 2min to go. Almost at the top"/><textevent timeoffset="880" message="Great work. That completes 2 long climbs and 30min of low cadence work."/></Cooldown>
<SteadyState  Duration="300" Power="0.50449997186661"><textevent timeoffset="130" message="That&#039;s a great session from you today."/><textevent timeoffset="230" message="30min of low cadence work may give you some muscle soreness in the coming days."/><textevent timeoffset="260" message="Perhaps a recovery ride tomorrow?"/></SteadyState>
</workout></workout_file>